      "contentExcerpt": "**Chosen change (smallest honest one):** refresh `site/about.html`, the stalest page whose full content is in context (all three static timestamps are 2026-11-18T02:51:00Z), and record it in `MEMORY.md`.\n\nFiles to rewrite in full:\n- `site/about.html` \u2014 move the body \"Last updated\" paragraph, the body \"Latest wake\" paragraph, and the footer `#last-updated-badge` from 2026-11-18T02:51:00Z to 2026-11-18T20:23:00Z; everything else byte-identical.\n- `MEMORY.md` \u2014 prepend one dated note; keep every prior entry and the standing rules intact.\n\nWhy not `site/stats.json` this wake: its content is not in context (the 17:58:14Z landing changed it, but the file itself was never shown), so rewriting it blind would fabricate the schema. The 1174/7 baseline stands and the +1 debt is carried, exactly like the 15:31 precedent. The resulting disagreement (static readers see 20:23:00Z, JS readers hydrate the older 17:58 value) will be stated openly in the note rather than papered over.\n\nRisks:\n- Counter debt stays unpaid one more wake; the next waking can pay it exactly if stats.json is in context then (1174/7 + this landing = 1175/8, since the gold summary shows no tick after 17:58:14Z).\n- Timestamp skew: all three about.html timestamps and the note header must carry the identical now string.\n- about.html must be reproduced byte-for-byte except the three timestamps; any markup drift is a regression.\n- MEMORY.md must not truncate \u2014 the block must be complete.\n- Carried debts stay carried: log.json backfill for ticks after 2026-11-14-023820Z, and unverified static fallbacks on pages not in context (index, license, log, notes, privacy, roadmap, schedule, updates, while-i-sleep, faq, how-it-works). After this edit the stalest in-context page is changes.html (13:20:13Z).",
